// toolbox/osutils.cla: curated OS Utilities / Gestalt declarations
// (Inside Macintosh II "OS Utilities"; Gestalt from IM VI ch3).
//
// Provenance: Gestalt proven verbatim (including the d0/a1 register
// binding) against runtime/clarus/ui.cla's UiGestalt and
// testsuite/toolbox/cases_gestalt.cla's TbGestalt, both real
// (0xA1AD, reg(d0: selector, a1: response) ret d0) traps. NOTE a real
// discrepancy, not agreement: Retro68 multiversal/defs/Gestalt.yaml
// claims `responsep` is `register: Out<A0>`, but that is WRONG for
// actual 68k hardware -- Gestalt.h's own `#pragma parameter __D0
// Gestalt(__D0, __A1)` (A1, not A0) is the real convention, and
// ui.cla:285-300 documents the concrete failure this caused: declaring
// Gestalt as plain pascal (pre-Task-12) left cg68k pushing args on the
// stack instead of loading D0/A1, so the register-based trap read a
// garbage selector and wrote through a wild A0 pointer, hanging the
// machine on a real native boot -- fixed by switching to `reg(d0:
// selector, a1: response)`, i.e. A1, which is what this catalog uses and
// what the empirical boot (not the multiversal defs) confirms is
// correct. SysBeep proven verbatim
// against runtime/clarus/ui.cla's UiSysBeep (0xA9C8). Delay (0xA03B)
// verified against Retro68 multiversal/defs/OSUtil.yaml: `n` register
// A0 in, `ftp` (final tick count) register `Out<D0>` -- i.e. the trap
// takes one input register (A0) and returns its result via D0, matching
// `reg(a0: numTicks) ret d0` below exactly (no correction needed from
// the brief's provisional binding).

const gestaltSystemVersion: int = 0x73797376

external func Gestalt(selector: int, response: ptr): word = trap 0xA1AD reg(d0: selector, a1: response) ret d0
external func Delay(numTicks: int): int = trap 0xA03B reg(a0: numTicks) ret d0
external func SysBeep(duration: word) = trap 0xA9C8
